==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|en}}. Originally a local name for the disease in {{w|Dorset}} and {{w|Somerset}}, England. Occasionally postulated to be derived from a Dorsetian dialectal term {{m|en|*rucket||to breathe with difficulty, wheeze}}, but the semantic connection is tenuous. See {{m|en|rachitis}}, but the medical name was chosen purposefully by English physician {{w|Daniel Whistler}} from phonetic similarity to ''rickets''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɪkəts/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A [[disorder]] of [[infancy]] and early [[childhood]] caused by a [[deficiency]] of [[vitamin D]], causing soft bones.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|rachitis}}, {{l|en|rhachitis}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|ricketiness}}
* {{l|en|rickety}}

